1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Breathe in. Breathe out. Look at the grass.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Is that a bug? No. That's a tiny rock. ...I shall eat it anyway.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Why do my feet look like dinosaur feet? Wait... am I a dinosaur?

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
If I peck this leaf 400 times, will it turn into bread? Worth a shot.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
The Giant Featherless Biped approaches. Does it hold the Red Bucket of Joy?

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
IT DOES NOT HOLD THE BUCKET. False alarm. Traitor.

7
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Look at Brenda over there. She thinks she's so special cause she laid an extra-oval egg today. Show-off.

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Target locked: juicy wriggling brown line in dirt. Initiate wiggle-butt jump.

9
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
MISSED. It was a root. My disappointment is immeasurable.

10
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Wait, where are my children? ...Oh right, I haven't sat on anything for 3 weeks.

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:08,000
If I step left, then right, then bob my head real fast... yes, physics checks out. I am smooth.

12
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
SHADOW! SKY MONSTER! ABORT! RETREAT! EVACUATE!

13
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Never mind. It was just an maple leaf falling. Stay calm. Maintain chicken dignity.

14
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:47,000
I'm telling you, the lawnmower is an ancient deity. It roars and consumes green souls.

15
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Peck. Peck. Scratch scratch. Peck. This is my entire career and I'm killing it.

16
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Sometimes I wonder... what if there's more to life than scratching dirt? What if... there's mulch?

17
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Gary is staring at me. Stop staring, Gary. You look like a feather duster with an attitude.

18
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:12,000
EGG ALERT. EGG ALERT. INCOMING SPHERICAL OBJECT. PREPARE THE BIRD CAVITY.

19
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Bawk... BAWK... BAAAWK! IT HAS ARRIVED! BEHOLD MY ARTWORK!

20
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Why did I scream? I don't know. It's in the contract.

21
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:57,000
The Giant Human took my artwork. I am outraged. ...Ooh, a piece of old cabbage!

22
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Dust bath time. Throw the dirt on the back. Yes. Pure luxury. 5-star spa experience.

23
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:48,000
If I peck the wooden post at 60 Hertz, does it resonate with the cosmic frequency of corn?

24
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:16,000
One step... two step... stop. Freeze. Did the wind just insult my crest?

25
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:47,000
I have a dream. A dream where scratch is infinite and wire fences are purely ornamental.

26
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Hold on. Why *did* the ancestor cross the road? Was there corn? Was it fleeing Gary?

27
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Look at that shiny thing on the ground. A bottle cap? A sacred amulet? *Gulp* Tastes metal.

28
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:18,000
I'm going to run in a circle for no apparent reason at maximum velocity. WATCH ME GOOOOO!

29
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Phew. Cardio done for the week. Time to stare blankly into the middle distance.

30
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Brenda is sitting in my favorite nest box. I will stand 2 inches away and glare intensely.

31
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Glaring status: Unsuccessful. Brenda is immune to my mind rays.

32
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Human has returned. Hands behind back. What's in the hands? IS IT MEALWORMS?

33
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:35,000
MEALWORMS! CODE RED! VIOLENT PECKING PROTOCOL ACTIVATED!

34
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:51,000
FIGHT! FIGHT FOR THE DRIED WORMS! THERE ARE NO FRIENDS AT DIRT LEVEL!

35
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:17,000
I snatched three. Victory is sweet. I will now hide under the ramp and swallow them whole.

36
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Munch munch. Tastes like crunchy dirt. 10/10 recommendation.

37
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Did you see that twitch? My left eye saw a butterfly, my right eye saw a dark void. Balance.

38
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:16,000
I should write a book. 'Pecked: My Story of Grain and Betrayal.'

39
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:57,000
What is water? Cold liquid dirt. I sip, I look at sky, I swallow. Divine.

40
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:48,000
The cat is watching me. Little does it know, my lineage fought velociraptors. Come at me, fluffball.

41
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Cat walked away. Another glorious victory for the Dinosaur Dynasty.

42
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Why is my tail twitching? Is it sending Morse code to the Mothership?

43
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Scratch left, scratch right, step back, peck. Repeat until world ends.

44
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:08,000
I suspect the rooster doesn't actually control the sun. But I'm too polite to bring it up in group therapy.

45
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
A fly! An aerial target! Intercept sequence initiated!

46
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:19,000
Missed. The fly mocked my lack of aerodynamics.

47
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:07,000
My feathers look fabulous today. A delicate blend of copper and dust.

48
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:08,000
What if the fence isn't keeping us in... but keeping the outside world out from OUR POWER?

49
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Deep thought. Very deep. Now back to eating this styrofoam cup I found behind the shed.

50
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Human said 'Good morning, ladies.' I am a majestic creature, not just a 'lady.'

51
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:07,000
Oh look, a worm! ...Wait, it's a string. Tastes like string. Delicious.

52
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
If I tilt my head 90 degrees, the shed looks like a diamond. Science is amazing.

53
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:08,000
Gary tried to crow again. Sounded like a dying bagpipe. Absolutely embarrassing for the flock.

54
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:07,000
I have decided: I am the Queen of this patch of clover. Bow before my majestic waddle.

55
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Sun beam detected on porch. Commencing operational nap protocol.

56
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:05,000
Zzz... infinite mealworms falling from sky... zzz...

57
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
SNORT. I'm awake! Who said that? Was it the squirrel? I don't trust squirrels.

58
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:08,000
Squirrels are just tail-heavy rats with better PR. Stay off my lawn, nut-hoarder.

59
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:07,000
Another egg feeling... Wait, false alarm. Just gas from yesterday's stolen apple core.

60
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Scratch scratch. Is that a beetle? No, acorn cap. Tricked again by mother nature.

61
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:07,000
I wonder what the big blue ceiling is made of. Soft cotton? Blueberry yogurt?

62
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Rain drop! WE ARE UNDER ATTACK FROM HIGH ALTITUDE WATER BOMBS!

63
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:08,000
Run to coop! Save the feathers! Every chicken for herself!

64
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:07,000
Huddling together. Smell of damp feathers. Truly the height of chicken civilization.

65
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Rain stopped. The sun returns! I survived the Great Deluge of 2:15 PM!

66
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:08,000
Mud puddles! The ground has transformed into gourmet soup! TIME TO SIP!

67
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Human is walking toward the coop door with the evening latch...

68
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:07,000
No! Not bedtime yet! The sun is still slightly above the tree line! FREEDOM!

69
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Okay fine, roosting bar looks pretty comfy actually. I claim the top spot!

70
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:07,000
Brenda is trying to push me off. I will deploy the Sharp Beak Defense mechanism.

71
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Settled. Wing over wing. Head tucked into neck fluff. Maximum compactness achieved.

72
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:08,000
Darkness falls. The coop is silent. Tomorrow... we peck the world again.

73
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Final thought before sleep: Corn is love. Corn is life. Goodnight, world.

